{
 "_readme": [
  "Board slugs deliberately removed from board-slugs.json because their list endpoint",
  "returns a definitive 404. This file is the RECORD of that decision, and it has two jobs.",
  "",
  "1. It stops a re-harvest silently resurrecting them. board-slugs.json is derived from",
  "   Simplify's listings.json by simplify::extract_board_slugs. Nothing in that pipeline",
  "   knows a slug was retired, so without this file the next harvest re-adds all of them and",
  "   we go back to polling dead boards forever.",
  "",
  "2. It keeps migration 0028 honest. 0028 tagged sightings with scopes, and",
  "   scope_backfill's `every_slug_named_is_one_the_board_directory_actually_polls` asserts",
  "   every slug it names is still polled -- the failure being a tag pointing at a board",
  "   nothing fetches, which never advances again. Retiring a slug necessarily breaks that",
  "   assertion, so the test now accepts a slug that appears HERE instead. The exception is",
  "   explicit and reviewable rather than the assertion being weakened.",
  "",
  "A slug earns a place here by 404ing on RETIREMENT_RUNS consecutive verdicts with no answer",
  "in between -- see internships::board_retirement. One 404 is not evidence; a 404 can be a",
  "deploy, a rename in flight, or a CDN with an opinion.",
  "",
  "Removing a slug is not free: under scoped expiry a retired board produces no completed",
  "scope, so any sighting still tagged to it stops advancing. Before retiring, check that",
  "nothing live depends on it. On 2026-09-05 exactly one did -- greenhouse/glossgenius, whose",
  "two sightings were already expired at 9 consecutive misses, so nothing was stranded."
 ],
